      "title_s":["AUTOSAFE 2.0: Improved and Optimized Automation of Fault Tree Analysis"],
      "abstract_s":["Fault Tree Analysis (FTA) is widely used for safety certification of complex cyber-physical systems, yet its manual application is time-consuming and error-prone. This paper presents AUTOSAFE 2.0, a web-based tool for automated fault tree generation from model-based system descriptions, extending the Open Avionics Architecture Model with explicit failure propagation semantics. Key improvements include optimized synthesis using Binary Decision Diagrams, automated propagation-combination generation, integrated model verification, and XML-based interoperability with industrial tools such as Isograph. Work in progress targets extended industrial validation, deeper regulatory alignment, and automated hazard analysis integration."],
